try></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOGA NOBUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KURIBAYASHI MITSURU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MAEDA HIROYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIGO, NARUHITO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOGA, NOBUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KURIBAYASHI, MITSURU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MAEDA, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An electrode structure for iontophoresis devices that is superior in economics, operability, stability and safety, and a method of producing the same.  An electrode structure for iontophoresis devices has a backing that comprises base films (1) having forming portions, electrode layers (14, 15) on the anode and cathode sides formed to extend from the inner bottoms of the forming portions and through the outer peripheries, and insulation layers (3) each formed around the outer periphery of the forming portion.  The forming portions of this backing have recesses, where electrically conductive layers (12, 13) on the anode and cathode sides are disposed.  Covers (8) are provided for sealing these electrically conductive layers (12, 13) between them and the insulation layers (3).  The back of each base film (1) is provided with a skin-applied adhesive sheet (10), and adhesive sheet liners (16) are disposed on the covers (8).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une structure d'électrode destinée à des dispositifs d'ionophorèse, cette structure d'électrode possédant des propriétés supérieures en termes de coût, d'exploitabilité, de stabilité et de sécurité. L'invention concerne également le procédé de production de cette structure. La structure d'électrode destinée aux dispositifs d'ionophorèse comprend un support comportant des couches (1) de base dotées de parties de formation, des couches (14, 15) d'électrode des côtés de l'anode et de la cathode formées de manière à se projeter à partir des fonds intérieurs des parties de formation et par les pourtours extérieurs, et des couches isolantes (3) formées chacune autour du pourtour extérieur de la partie de formation. Les parties de formation de ce support présentent des creux dans lesquels sont disposées des couches conductrices (12, 13) des côtés de l'anode et de la cathode. Des couvercles (8) sont destinés à former un scellement entre les couches conductrices (12, 13) et les couches isolantes (3). Le support de chaque couche (1) de base comporte une feuille adhésive (10) appliquée à la surface, des doublures (16) de feuilles adhésives étant disposées sur les couvercles (8).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>